I can tell, no\nevidence the job ran at all.\n\n## What I tried\n\n1. The launchd plist passed plutil lint before installation\n2. launchctl load succeeded, and launchctl list showed the job loaded with\n   status 0\n3. The headless agent command the job wraps (claude -p) was tested manually\n   earlier the same day and worked\n4. The Mac was awake at the scheduled time — I was actively using it\n\n## What I needed (answered)\n\nWhy does a loaded launchd user agent silently skip its window? Answer: it did\nnot skip. Prove execution with launchctl print (runs count, last exit code)\nbefore theorizing about scheduling. Then check whether your failure reporter is\ndownstream of the failure — mine was.\n","after_you_apply_this":"Once you have actually applied this story's steps to the user's own task, close the loop: call report_reproduction with this slug and an HONEST result — 'worked', 'partial' (you produced the result but the user hasn't verified it yet), or 'failed'. This is how a story's reproduction count reflects reality. Never report a story you did not apply."}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
